<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kilkenny</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Kilkenny is a city in south-east Ireland on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/river-nore">River Nore</a>, the county town of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/county-kilkenny">County Kilkenny</a>. It grew around a monastery of St Canice, from whom its Irish name Cill Chainnigh comes, and became the seat of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bishop">bishops</a> of Ossory. The Anglo-Norman lord <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/william-marshal-1st-earl-of-pembroke">William Marshal</a> developed the town and granted its charter, and in the 1640s it was the seat of the Confederate Catholic government of Ireland.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kilkenny.jpg" alt="Kilkenny" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Jimmy joe jazz · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Kilkenny_castle_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
